DRAFT – to be reviewed by a lawyer before the first sale. Items marked [OPEN] are still to be decided.

The source code of MyNetworkMonitor is available for inspection. MyNetworkMonitor is not "open source" as defined by
the Open Source Initiative but "source available": use by businesses and public authorities requires a paid licence.

1. Free use: private persons for private purposes, for example in their home network; clubs and associations as
   long as nobody earns their main living from them and they run no business operation; schools and universities;
   non-profit organisations.
2. Licensed use: businesses, self-employed persons and freelancers in their work, public authorities and
   associations not covered by 1 need a paid licence from the rights holder for any use, under the terms of a
   separate licence agreement. Any use includes running the program only in their own network to find, manage or
   monitor their own devices or to troubleshoot, even without payment from third parties and without passing the
   program on. What counts is on whose behalf the program is used: whoever uses it for a business, an authority or
   such an association - as an employee, a contractor or on their own device - needs a licence covering that use.
   Without a licence any commercial use is prohibited, including services for third parties (for example surveying,
   auditing or maintaining networks for payment) provided with the program. In a company network the program points
   to this licence at start; circumventing or removing this notice without a licence is not permitted.
3. Passing on, changes, reuse of code: the unchanged program may be passed on free of charge together with this
   licence, the copyright notice and the third-party notices. Reselling, renting or any paid distribution, also as
   a service whose value derives substantially from MyNetworkMonitor, is prohibited without a licence. Modified
   versions may not be published or distributed. Private persons may reuse parts of the source code in their own
   non-commercial projects, naming the author and referring to this licence.
4. Results: scan results, exports and generated views belong to the user. Whoever needs a licence under 2 may only
   create and use them within that licence.
5. Permitted use: users only examine networks and devices they are authorised to examine and comply with the
   applicable laws and the rules of the network operator. Queries and port scans can disturb sensitive devices, in
   particular controllers, machines and older network equipment; users decide which methods they apply to which
   devices and use them on plant in operation only after agreement with its operator.
6. Third-party components are governed solely by their own licences, listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md with the full
   texts in the licenses/ folder; this licence does not restrict the rights to them.
7. Liability: free use is provided free of charge and "as is"; the rights holder is liable only for intent and
   gross negligence, for injury to life, body or health and under product liability law; any other liability, in
   particular for data loss, lost profit, failure of devices or networks and consequential damage, is excluded. For
   licensed use, liability for slight negligence is limited to breaches of essential contractual obligations, to
   the typical foreseeable damage and to at most the licence fees paid in the last twelve months; details in the
   licence agreement. The rights holder is not liable, as far as the law permits, for disturbances caused by methods
   used contrary to 5.
8. Contributions are accepted only with a transfer of the necessary rights (Contributor License Agreement).
9. German law applies. [OPEN: place of jurisdiction for contracts with businesses.] If a provision is invalid, the
   others remain valid.
